\description{
Fits a PWM (and a spatial model) that predicts \code{response} from \code{sequences}.
The function operates in one of three modes depending on its arguments:
}
\details{
\describe{
\item{Single motif from a fixed seed (\code{motif} given):}{One PWM is optimized
starting from the supplied kmer or PSSM. Returns a single regression result.}
\item{Single motif from a kmer screen (\code{motif = NULL}, \code{multi_kmers = TRUE}, default):}{
Candidate kmer seeds are generated by \code{screen_kmers}, each is regressed on
a train/validation split, the best by validation score is refit on the full
data. Returns a single regression result. Set \code{return_all = TRUE} to get
\emph{all} candidate-kmer regressions instead of just the best - useful when you
want the top N motifs without the residual-rounds approach used by
\code{motif_num > 1}.}
\item{Multiple motifs via residual rounds (\code{motif_num > 1}):}{Delegates to
\code{\link{regress_multiple_motifs}}. Each successive motif is fit against the
residual of a linear model of the previous motifs. Returns a multi-motif result
